From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] pcm: keep dmix and dsnoop on one ReliefOS hardware lease

ReliefOS exposes one physical HDA stream lease for each logical playback
and capture endpoint.  The direct plugins' legacy server mode is the ALSA
mechanism for sharing that lease between independent clients; without it,
newer PCM protocol versions make every secondary client reopen the hardware
PCM and receive EBUSY from the endpoint lease.

---
 src/pcm/pcm_direct.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/pcm/pcm_direct.c b/src/pcm/pcm_direct.c
--- a/src/pcm/pcm_direct.c
+++ b/src/pcm/pcm_direct.c
@@ -1452,8 +1452,11 @@
 	{
 		int ver = 0;
 		ioctl(spcm->poll_fd, SNDRV_PCM_IOCTL_PVERSION, &ver);
-		if (ver < SNDRV_PROTOCOL_VERSION(2, 0, 8))
-			dmix->shmptr->use_server = 1;
+		/* ReliefOS keeps one physical HDA lease per endpoint.  Use the
+		 * upstream direct server so secondary dmix/dsnoop clients share that
+		 * lease instead of reopening the hardware PCM. */
+		if (ver >= 0)
+			dmix->shmptr->use_server = 1;
 	}
